{
    "chapter_num": 9,
    "verses_count": 11,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Wicked Are Slain"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then He called out in my hearing with a loud voice, saying, “Let those who have charge over the city draw near, each "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "with"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " a "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or destroying"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "deadly weapon in his hand.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And suddenly six men came from the direction of the upper gate, which faces north, each with his "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. shattering weapon"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "battle-ax in his hand. One man among them "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " clothed with linen and had a writer’s inkhorn "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. upon his loins"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "at his side. They went in and stood beside the bronze altar."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now the glory of the God of Israel had gone up from the cherub, where it had been, to the threshold of the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. house"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "temple. And He called to the man clothed with linen, who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "had"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the writer’s inkhorn at his side; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " said to him, “Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and put a mark on the foreheads of the men who sigh and cry over all the abominations that are done within it.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "To the others He said in my "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. ears"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "hearing, “Go after him through the city and kill;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. strike"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " do not let your eye spare, nor have any pity. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Utterly"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Slay to destruction"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " slay old "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " young men, maidens and little children and women; but do not come near anyone on whom "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the mark; and begin at My sanctuary.” So they began with the elders who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " before the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. house"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "temple. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then He said to them, “Defile the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. house"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "temple, and fill the courts with the slain. Go out!” And they went out and killed in the city."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So it was, that while they were killing them, I was left "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "alone;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and I fell on my face and cried out, and said, “Ah, Lord "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "God"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "! Will You destroy all the remnant of Israel in pouring out Your fury on Jerusalem?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then He said to me, “The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " exceedingly great, and the land is full of bloodshed, and the city full of perversity; for they say, ‘The "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " has forsaken the land, and the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " does not see!’ "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And as for Me also, My eye will neither spare, nor will I have pity, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "but"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " I will recompense their deeds on their own head.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Just then, the man clothed with linen, who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "had"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the inkhorn at his side, reported back and said, “I have done as You commanded me.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}